        "original_id": "70ae94b3-8e66-5e41-a053-9bbcf6be0c37",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Brown, Jhené Aiko, James Fauntleroy, Mike Posner, Lil Wayne, Rick Ross, DJ Khaled, Big Sean, Tyga, 2 Chainz, The Game, Jadakiss\n- Groups: B2K, The Olympicks, Triple C's\n- Projects: Detroit, I Am Not a Human Being, Teflon Don, Custom Cars & Cycles, Kiss The Ring, Hotel California\n- Places: Detroit, Michigan\n- Topics: music careers, guest appearances, music production\n\nFacts:\n- Jhené Aiko began her music career by contributing vocals and appearing in several music videos for the R&B group B2K.\n- The Olympicks originated in Detroit, Michigan.\n- The Olympicks worked on hip-hop projects including Lil Wayne's I Am Not a Human Being, Rick Ross' Teflon Don, Triple C's Custom Cars & Cycles, DJ Khaled's Kiss The Ring, and Big Sean's Detroit mixtape.\n- Big Sean's Detroit mixtape includes American singers Chris Brown, Jhené Aiko, James Fauntleroy, and Mike Posner.\n- Tyga's album Hotel California features guest appearances from Lil Wayne, 2 Chainz, The Game, and Jadakiss.\n- Tyga's album Hotel California had production handled by DJ Mustard, Detail, Cool & Dre, David D.A. Doman, Mars of 1500 or Nothin', The Olympicks, SAP, and Ryan Hunt, among others.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
